# Every binary asset type in the repo, declared binary rather than left to git's guess. Git calls a
# file text when it has no NUL and few non-printable bytes, and the Windows runner checks out with
# core.autocrlf=true, which then rewrites each 0x0A into 0x0D 0x0A. Small NUL-free images pass that
# guess: LinePatterns/4.ppm had its header newlines turned into CRLF, which shifted every pixel a
# byte and broke line_patterns against C++ AGG on Windows only (EmbeddedImageIntegrityTests guards
# the demo's pictures). STLs here are ASCII but are left binary too, so a mesh read on Windows is
# the mesh that was committed.
*.ppm binary
*.raw binary
*.bmp binary
*.png binary
*.tga binary
*.ttf binary
*.stl binary
*.zip binary
*.dll binary

# The LCD byte-exactness fixture is raw coverage/pixel dumps whose whole point is that every byte
# survives the round trip. Git's automatic binary detection looks for a NUL byte, and some of these
# blobs legitimately contain none (star_nonzero.dst is fully opaque, so no channel is ever 0, and the
# LcdBuffer planes are cleared to a non-zero background), which would let core.autocrlf treat them as
# text and rewrite every 0x0A into 0x0D 0x0A on checkout - silently corrupting the reference the port
# is compared against. Declare them binary explicitly.
TestData/LcdFixture/*.lcd binary
TestData/LcdFixture/*.gray binary
TestData/LcdFixture/*.dst binary
TestData/LcdFixture/*.bufcolor binary
TestData/LcdFixture/*.bufalpha binary

# The manifest beside them is text and is meant to stay readable in a diff. Pinning it to LF keeps
# the working-tree bytes identical to what the Rust generator writes, so regenerating the fixture
# never shows up as whole-file line-ending churn.
TestData/LcdFixture/manifest.txt text eol=lf

# mol_view's molecule file (examples/AggSharpDemo/AggSharpDemo/Art/1.sdf) is text, and both parsers take
# CRLF, but LF everywhere keeps the checked-out bytes those of C++ AGG's copy on every OS.
*.sdf text eol=lf

# The SVG Test window's resvg-test-suite samples are compared against reference renders; LF keeps
# the bytes the renderer parses identical to upstream's on every OS.
*.svg text eol=lf
